      ],
      "id": "68ba833f-6fd4-41d4-9521-0531c752e866",
      "name": "Build Evidence Package"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// Build Guide S11: clearly separated evidence package, never let the\n// model guess. Everything below TASK is the only thing it may reason from.\nconst p = $json.evidence_package;\n\nconst prompt = `ALERT OBSERVATIONS (directly from Wazuh - treat as fact)\n${JSON.stringify(p.alert, null, 2)}\n\nVERIFIED MITRE ATT&CK CONTEXT (resolved locally, safe to cite)\n${JSON.stringify(p.enrichment.mitre_verified, null, 2)}\n\nUNVERIFIED MITRE IDS (present in alert, NOT confirmed - flag, do not treat as fact)\n${JSON.stringify(p.enrichment.mitre_unresolved, null, 2)}\n\nVERIFIED CVE CONTEXT (from NVD, safe to cite if status is VERIFIED)\n${JSON.stringify(p.enrichment.cve_context, null, 2)}\n\nKNOWN UNKNOWNS (missing from this alert - never fabricate these)\n${JSON.stringify(p.known_unknowns, null, 2)}\n\nTASK\nYou are mentoring a junior SOC analyst who has never seen this alert type before.\nUsing ONLY the evidence above, produce a guided triage analysis as the required JSON.\nEvery suspicious_indicator and key_evidence item must point to something actually\npresent in ALERT OBSERVATIONS or VERIFIED context above - never invent details.\nWhere something is not observable, say so explicitly instead of guessing.`;\n\nreturn { json: { ...$json, llm_prompt: prompt } };"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
