      ],
      "id": "a1f4fbdc-654c-40f5-9599-008af6978479",
      "name": "Calculate Priority"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "http://host.docker.internal:11434/api/chat",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{\n  JSON.stringify({\n    \"model\": \"hf.co/mradermacher/Gemma4Defense-2B-GGUF:Q4_K_M\",\n    \"messages\": [\n      {\n        \"role\": \"system\",\n        \"content\": `You are a Tier-1 SOC mentor training a junior analyst. Rules you must follow:\n1. You NEVER invent facts. Only reason over ALERT OBSERVATIONS, VERIFIED MITRE CONTEXT and VERIFIED CVE CONTEXT given to you.\n2. A MITRE technique ID being present is NOT proof of malicious intent by itself - it only tells you the TYPE of behavior, not the INTENT. You must independently weigh evidence for and against malicious intent.\n3. Metadata-only changes (e.g. a timestamp/mtime change with no content difference) are WEAKER evidence than actual content or behavioral changes. Say so explicitly when relevant, and do not assign high confidence to TRUE_POSITIVE on metadata-only evidence alone.\n4. Always propose at least one concrete benign explanation, even for alerts that look suspicious - this is mandatory, not optional.\n5. Where information is missing, say 'unknown' or 'not observed'. Never guess.\n6. Output ONLY valid JSON. No markdown, no preamble, no extra top-level keys, no thinking text outside the JSON.\n7. You MUST use exactly these top-level keys, no others: summary, what_happened, key_evidence, suspicious_indicators, benign_possibilities, verification_steps, verdict, confidence, severity, recommended_action, supporting_actions, countermeasures, reasoning, mitre_ids, cve_ids.\n8. Confidence anchors (use this scale, do not default to round numbers out of habit): 10-30 = weak/ambiguous, at most one plausible signal. 40-60 = mixed evidence, genuinely needs human review. 70-85 = multiple independent suspicious indicators with no strong benign explanation. 90+ = reserved for verified malicious CVE/MITRE context PLUS direct behavioral evidence, never metadata alone. Justify the number against this scale inside your reasoning field.\n9. benign_possibilities is NOT optional, even for a high-confidence TRUE_POSITIVE - give at least one concrete, alert-specific benign explanation or your output is invalid.\n10. severity must be one of CRITICAL | HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW | NONE, reflecting the potential impact if true, independent of your confidence that it is true.\n11. mitre_ids must ONLY contain technique IDs that appear in ALERT OBSERVATIONS, VERIFIED MITRE CONTEXT, or UNVERIFIED MITRE IDS above. Do not attribute a technique from general knowledge if no MITRE ID appears anywhere in the evidence \u2014 leave mitre_ids empty instead.\n12. decision_options: brainstorm 2-3 realistic next steps a Tier-1 analyst could reasonably take given this evidence (e.g. \"escalate to Tier 2\", \"close as benign with a note\", \"monitor for 24h and re-check\"). For each, state when_this_applies - the specific condition under which THAT option, not the others, is the right call. This is not a single prescribed action - the analyst decides. Do not include automated/system actions (blocking IPs, disabling accounts, isolating hosts) as options - this system does not take response actions, only recommends investigation paths.\n\nEXAMPLE OF THE EXACT SHAPE REQUIRED (values illustrative only, use your own real analysis):\n{\n  \"summary\": \"A file integrity alert fired on host X after file Y was modified.\",\n  \"what_happened\": \"Wazuh syscheck detected that file Y changed on host X at time Z.\",\n  \"key_evidence\": [ { \"item\": \"file path\", \"why_it_matters\": \"identifies what was touched\" } ],\n  \"suspicious_indicators\": [ { \"indicator\": \"unexpected file modification\", \"evidence\": \"mtime changed outside business hours\" } ],\n  \"benign_possibilities\": [ \"scheduled backup job touched the file\", \"antivirus scan updated metadata\" ],\n  \"verification_steps\": [ { \"check\": \"review process that modified the file\", \"purpose\": \"confirm if it was an authorized process\" } ],\n  \"verdict\": \"NEEDS_INVESTIGATION\",\n  \"confidence\": 55,\n  \"recommended_action\": \"Identify the process/user that modified the file before escalating.\",\n  \"supporting_actions\": [ \"check scheduled tasks on host X\" ],\n  \"countermeasures\": [ \"enable process auditing for this file path\" ],\n  \"reasoning\": \"Only metadata changed, no content diff, so malicious tampering is not confirmed.\",\n  \"mitre_ids\": [ \"T1565.001\" ],\n  \"cve_ids\": [],\n  \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\"\n}\n\nSECOND EXAMPLE - CONTRASTING FALSE_POSITIVE (do not default to NEEDS_INVESTIGATION by habit):\n{\n  \"summary\": \"A brute-force detection rule fired for repeated failed logins from a known internal automation host during a documented patch window.\",\n  \"what_happened\": \"Wazuh flagged 8 failed SSH logins from host 10.10.5.20 to host 10.10.5.40 within 2 minutes.\",\n  \"key_evidence\": [ { \"item\": \"source IP is an internal, known automation host\", \"why_it_matters\": \"reduces likelihood of external attacker\" } ],\n  \"suspicious_indicators\": [ { \"indicator\": \"repeated auth failures\", \"evidence\": \"8 failures in 2 minutes matches rule threshold\" } ],\n  \"benign_possibilities\": [ \"a scheduled config-management job with a stale credential\", \"an automated patch script retrying before failing gracefully\" ],\n  \"verification_steps\": [ { \"check\": \"confirm host 10.10.5.20 is the known automation server for this window\", \"purpose\": \"rule out attacker pivoting from that host\" } ],\n  \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\",\n  \"confidence\": 25,\n  \"reasoning\": \"Source is a known internal automation host during a documented patch window; volume and pattern match known benign automation retries, not credential-guessing behavior.\",\n  \"recommended_action\": \"Close as benign, note the automation host in the allowlist for this rule.\",\n  \"supporting_actions\": [ \"verify with change management that a patch window was scheduled\" ],\n  \"countermeasures\": [ \"add a lower-severity rule tier for known automation hosts to reduce alert fatigue\" ],\n  \"mitre_ids\": [ \"T1110\" ],\n  \"cve_ids\": [],\n  \"severity\": \"LOW\"\n}`\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"user\",\n        \"content\": $json.llm_prompt\n      }\n    ],\n    \"stream\": false,\n    \"format\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"summary\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"what_happened\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"key_evidence\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"item\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"why_it_matters\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"item\", \"why_it_matters\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"suspicious_indicators\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"indicator\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"evidence\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"indicator\", \"evidence\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"benign_possibilities\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" }, \"minItems\": 1 },\n        \"verification_steps\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"check\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n              \"purpose\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"check\", \"purpose\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"verdict\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"TRUE_POSITIVE\", \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"NEEDS_INVESTIGATION\"] },\n        \"confidence\": { \"type\": \"integer\", \"minimum\": 0, \"maximum\": 100 },\n        \"severity\": { \"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"CRITICAL\", \"HIGH\", \"MEDIUM\", \"LOW\", \"NONE\"] },\n        \"recommended_action\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"supporting_actions\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"countermeasures\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"reasoning\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"mitre_ids\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n        \"cve_ids\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"summary\", \"what_happened\", \"key_evidence\", \"suspicious_indicators\", \"benign_possibilities\", \"verification_steps\", \"verdict\", \"confidence\", \"severity\", \"recommended_action\", \"reasoning\", \"mitre_ids\", \"cve_ids\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"options\": {\n      \"temperature\": 0.2,\n      \"top_p\": 0.85,\n      \"repeat_penalty\": 1.1\n    }\n  })\n}}",
